IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sat-dates`

-- State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) -- the rules a person bringing or answering a matter in the Tribunal
-- meets: Part 3 (jurisdiction and review: ss 15, 17, 19-23, 25, 26, 29(5)), Part 4 (procedure: ss 39, 41, 42(4), 44, 45,
-- 48, 49, 53, 55, 64(3), 66(5), 68, 74, 76, 78, 82, 84-88, 92, 93, 95-99, 103(3)) and Part 5 (appeals: ss 105, 106).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in sat-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("cannot", "is not admissible
-- ... unless", "does not apply ... unless", "only applies ... on", "has to be made within", "means", an "if" or "when"
-- condition that fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
-- The Tribunal's, a court's and the President's judgments ("satisfied", "considers", "believes", "appropriate") are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Periods "after the day on which" exclude that day
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md), and a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday (Interpretation Act 1984 (WA)
-- s 61(1)(e), fork F12).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004", State
-- of Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004`

§§ `Time limits -- the answer type and the regulative rules`

-- A time limit as the person meets it.
DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `the last day is` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    -- the period has not begun: the event it runs from has not happened yet
    `no time limit runs yet`
    -- the step is not open to the person at all on these facts
    `the step is not open to you`

-- The actors the text names whose time limits the encoding runs: the person in the seat (the applicant, the party, the
-- person entitled to review), the decision-maker (s 21(4)).
DECLARE `Actor` IS ONE OF
    `the person`
    `the decision-maker`

-- The steps with a time limit fixed by the Act.
DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    -- s 21(3): a written request to the decision-maker for a statement of reasons
    `request a statement of reasons`
    -- s 21(4), with s 23(2): the statement, or the notice that it would be false or misleading
    `provide the statement of reasons`
    -- s 78(1): a request that the Tribunal give its reasons in writing
    `request written reasons from the Tribunal`
    -- s 105(5): the application for leave to appeal
    `apply for leave to appeal`
    -- s 105(6): instituting the appeal once leave is granted
    `institute the appeal`

-- The Act's time limits as duties: the actor MUST take the step WITHIN the days allowed, LEST the time has passed.
-- WITHIN counts days from the day the period runs from (day 0), so a step on the last day is on time.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN `Actor`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor` `Step`
`the step must be taken` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the actor`
    MUST EXACTLY `the step`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the actor` BECAUSE "the time limit fixed by the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 has passed"

-- Runs the rule over one event (the step, on its day) or, where the step has not been taken, a wait until the day asked
-- about. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so FULFILLED means on time and
-- anything else too late. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN `Actor`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `was it taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trace of` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` `taken` `was it taken` `at` `the day number` `is fulfilled` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the step must be taken` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `was it taken`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the actor` `the step` `the day number`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day number`)

-- Whether the person can still take a step on a day, given the day the period runs from and the time limit. NOTHING
-- before the period's starting day (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent on a step taken before the event).
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`, `the starting day` IS A DATE, `the limit` IS A `Time limit`, `the day of the step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person can take` `the step` `running from` `the starting day` `under` `the limit` `on` `the day of the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `the step is not open to you` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `no time limit runs yet` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `the day of the step` `is before` `the starting day`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the trace of` `the person` `the step` `within` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `the final day`) `taken` TRUE `at` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `the day of the step`) `is fulfilled`)

§§ `Part 3 Division 1-3 -- which jurisdiction (ss 13-15, 17)`

DECLARE `Jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    -- s 15: a matter that does not involve a review of a decision, and a s 44(4) referral
    `original jurisdiction`
    -- s 17: a matter that expressly or necessarily involves a review of a decision, and a s 44(3) referral
    `review jurisdiction`

DECLARE `How the matter came` IS ONE OF
    -- s 13(1): a provision of an enabling Act lets an application be made to the Tribunal
    `under an enabling Act`
    -- s 44(3): the applicant asked the executive officer to refer the rejection of the application, or a condition
    `a referral of the rejection of my application or its conditions`
    -- s 44(4): the executive officer referred the question whether the application could be rejected
    `a referral by the executive officer of whether my application could be rejected`

GIVEN `how it came` IS A `How the matter came`, `does it involve a review of a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Jurisdiction`
`ss 15, 17 -- the jurisdiction` `how it came` `does it involve a review of a decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it came`
    WHEN `a referral of the rejection of my application or its conditions` THEN `review jurisdiction`
    WHEN `a referral by the executive officer of whether my application could be rejected` THEN `original jurisdiction`
    WHEN `under an enabling Act` THEN
        IF `does it involve a review of a decision`
        THEN `review jurisdiction`
        ELSE `original jurisdiction`

§§ `s 19 -- Tribunal review and judicial review`

-- s 19(3)(a), (c), (5): a Tribunal review "cannot be commenced at the same time as" judicial review proceedings, nor
-- "subsequently" once they have commenced, unless they were dismissed or struck out for a procedural defect, or as
-- inappropriate or because the Tribunal is more appropriate. TRUE means barred.
GIVEN `have judicial review proceedings been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were they commenced at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were they dismissed or struck out for a s 19(5) reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3)(a), (c), (5) -- a Tribunal review is barred` `have judicial review proceedings been commenced` `were they commenced at the same time` `were they dismissed or struck out for a s 19(5) reason` MEANS
    IF NOT `have judicial review proceedings been commenced`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `were they commenced at the same time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `were they dismissed or struck out for a s 19(5) reason`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 19(3)(b), (4): judicial review proceedings "cannot subsequently be commenced" once a Tribunal review has commenced,
-- during it and after it ends, unless it was struck out under s 50(1) because judicial review is more appropriate; and
-- the bar does not touch judicial review of the Tribunal's own decision. TRUE means barred.
GIVEN `has a Tribunal review been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was it struck out under s 50(1) for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it judicial review of the Tribunal's own decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3)(b), (4) -- judicial review is barred` `has a Tribunal review been commenced` `was it struck out under s 50(1) for judicial review` `is it judicial review of the Tribunal's own decision` MEANS
    IF `is it judicial review of the Tribunal's own decision`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `has a Tribunal review been commenced`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `was it struck out under s 50(1) for judicial review`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 2 -- information about the decision (ss 20-23)`

-- s 20(1), (2): the decision-maker "is to give" written notice of the decision and the review right, unless (a) the
-- decision does not adversely affect the person and either (i) is a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or
-- limitation or (ii) puts the person in the most favourable category of entitlement, or (b) it is prescribed. Where the
-- "unless" is met the answer is JUST FALSE (fork F3).
GIVEN `does it adversely affect my interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does it put me in the most favourable category` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1), (2) -- I must be given notice` `does it adversely affect my interests` `is it a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or limitation` `does it put me in the most favourable category` `is it prescribed by the regulations` MEANS
    IF     `is it prescribed by the regulations`
        OR (    (NOT `does it adversely affect my interests`)
            AND (   `is it a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or limitation`
                 OR `does it put me in the most favourable category`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 21(1), (2): the person may request a written statement of reasons unless (a) already given one with the reasons and
-- the findings of fact, or (b) the enabling Act gives its own entitlement to such a statement (fork F3).
GIVEN `have I already been given a statement of reasons and findings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act give its own right to reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21(1), (2) -- I may request reasons` `have I already been given a statement of reasons and findings` `does the enabling Act give its own right to reasons` IF
        (NOT `have I already been given a statement of reasons and findings`)
    AND (NOT `does the enabling Act give its own right to reasons`)

-- s 21(3): the request "can be made (a) at any time within the period of 28 days after the day on which the decision was
-- made; or (b) if section 20(1) applies, at any time before the expiration of the period of 28 days after the day on
-- which notice is given". Joined by "or", so the later of the two days (fork F4); where s 20(1) applies and no notice has
-- been given, (b)'s period has not begun.
GIVEN `may I request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `does s 20(1) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has notice been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 21(3) -- the time limit to request reasons` `may I request` `the day of the decision` `does s 20(1) apply` `has notice been given` `the day of the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `may I request`
    THEN `the step is not open to you`
    ELSE IF `does s 20(1) apply`
         THEN IF `has notice been given`
              THEN `the last day is` (`the later of` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`) `and` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the notice`))
              ELSE `no time limit runs yet`
         ELSE `the last day is` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`)

-- s 21(4): the decision-maker "is to comply with the request as soon as practicable, and in any case within the period of
-- 28 days after the request is made" (only the 28 days are encoded; "as soon as practicable" is a judgment, fork F5).
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(4) -- the last day for the statement` `the day of the request` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the request`

-- s 22(1): "if ..., contrary to section 21(4), the decisionmaker fails to provide the statement, the person may apply to
-- the Tribunal for an order". The decision-maker's duty is run as a regulative rule over what happened by the day of
-- applying. Before the 28 days are out there is no failure yet (JUST FALSE: the "if" fails). A s 23(2) notice (that the
-- statement would be false or misleading without protected matter) counts as compliance. A statement given late but
-- before the application still leaves a failure "contrary to section 21(4)" (fork F6).
GIVEN `may I request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE
      `has the decision-maker responded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the response` IS A DATE
      `the day of applying` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) -- I may apply for an order for reasons` `may I request` `the day of the request` `has the decision-maker responded` `the day of the response` `the day of applying` MEANS
    IF NOT `may I request`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT (`the day of applying` `is after` (`s 21(4) -- the last day for the statement` `the day of the request`))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST (NOT (`the trace of` `the decision-maker` `provide the statement of reasons` `within` 28 `taken` `responded by then` `at` `the response day number` `is fulfilled`))
    WHERE
        `responded by then` MEANS
                `has the decision-maker responded`
            AND (NOT (`the day of the response` `is after` `the day of applying`))
        `the response day number` MEANS
            IF `responded by then`
            THEN `the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day of the response`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day of applying`

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 3 -- the review (ss 25, 26, 29(5), 82)`

-- s 25(1): commencing a review "does not affect the operation of the decision ... unless (a) the enabling Act states
-- otherwise; or (b) the Tribunal makes an order under subsection (2)" (a stay). TRUE means the decision is stayed. Where
-- the enabling Act states otherwise, NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `has the Tribunal stayed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act state otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 -- the decision is stayed by the review` `has the Tribunal stayed the decision` `does the enabling Act state otherwise` MEANS
    IF `has the Tribunal stayed the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `does the enabling Act state otherwise`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 26: after the review commences the decision-maker "cannot (a) vary the decision; or (b) set [it] aside and substitute
-- its new decision, unless (c) that is permitted by the enabling Act; or (d) the parties to the proceeding consent; or
-- (e) the decisionmaker is invited under section 31 to reconsider the decision".
GIVEN `has the review commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act permit it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has the Tribunal invited reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- the decision-maker may change the decision` `has the review commenced` `does the enabling Act permit it` `do the parties consent` `has the Tribunal invited reconsideration` MEANS
    IF NOT `has the review commenced`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 26 speaks only after commencement)
    ELSE IF `does the enabling Act permit it` OR `do the parties consent` OR `has the Tribunal invited reconsideration`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `When the decision takes effect` IS ONE OF
    -- s 29(5)(b)
    `from when the reviewed decision would have had effect`
    -- s 29(5)(b) "unless the enabling Act states otherwise or the Tribunal orders otherwise"
    `as the enabling Act or the Tribunal's order says`
    -- s 82(1)
    `immediately it is given`
    `at the later time specified in it`

-- s 82(1): "comes into effect immediately after it is given, or at such later time as is specified in it, except as
-- otherwise provided in section 29(5)"; s 29(5)(b): a decision affirming, varying or substituted for the reviewed decision
-- has effect "from the time when the decision reviewed would have ... had effect" unless the enabling Act or the
-- Tribunal's order says otherwise.
GIVEN `is it an affirmed, varied or substituted decision on a review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act or an order say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the decision specify a later time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `When the decision takes effect`
`ss 29(5), 82 -- when the decision takes effect` `is it an affirmed, varied or substituted decision on a review` `does the enabling Act or an order say otherwise` `does the decision specify a later time` MEANS
    IF `is it an affirmed, varied or substituted decision on a review`
    THEN IF `does the enabling Act or an order say otherwise`
         THEN `as the enabling Act or the Tribunal's order says`
         ELSE `from when the reviewed decision would have had effect`
    ELSE IF `does the decision specify a later time`
         THEN `at the later time specified in it`
         ELSE `immediately it is given`

§§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- representation and interpreters (ss 39, 41, 93(3))`

-- s 39(1): a party may appear in person or be represented, "but a party cannot be represented by a person other than a
-- legal practitioner unless" (c)-(f) [(a) bodies corporate and (b) public sector bodies are not the individual's seat];
-- s 39(3): a person struck off or suspended "cannot represent a party"; s 39(4): the regulations or rules may exclude
-- persons; s 93(3): after a no legal representation election a party "cannot be represented by a legally qualified
-- person" (a lawyer, or someone the Tribunal thinks has qualifications or experience in law giving an advantage).
GIVEN `is the person a legal practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the person struck off or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the regulations or rules exclude the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was a no legal representation election made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the person otherwise a legally qualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `am I a party because of my public sector duties, represented by an authorised colleague` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the person have particular relevant knowledge or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has the Tribunal agreed, with its conditions met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the regulations or rules authorise it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39, s 93(3) -- the person may represent me` `is the person a legal practitioner` `is the person struck off or suspended` `do the regulations or rules exclude the person` `was a no legal representation election made` `is the person otherwise a legally qualified person` `am I a party because of my public sector duties, represented by an authorised colleague` `does the person have particular relevant knowledge or experience` `has the Tribunal agreed, with its conditions met` `do the regulations or rules authorise it` IF
        (NOT `is the person struck off or suspended`)
    AND (NOT `do the regulations or rules exclude the person`)
    AND (NOT (`was a no legal representation election made` AND (`is the person a legal practitioner` OR `is the person otherwise a legally qualified person`)))
    AND (   `is the person a legal practitioner`
         OR `am I a party because of my public sector duties, represented by an authorised colleague`
         OR `does the person have particular relevant knowledge or experience`
         OR `has the Tribunal agreed, with its conditions met`
         OR `do the regulations or rules authorise it`)

-- s 41: "Unless the Tribunal directs otherwise, a party ... may be assisted ... by an interpreter" (fork F3).
GIVEN `has the Tribunal directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 -- I may have an interpreter` `has the Tribunal directed otherwise` IF NOT `has the Tribunal directed otherwise`

§§ `Part 4 Division 2 -- commencing, rejection, copies, dismissal (ss 42, 44, 45, 48, 49, 53, 55)`

-- s 42(4): proceedings "cannot be commenced by 2 or more persons jointly unless the facts or circumstances relating to
-- each person's interests are the same or related".
GIVEN `are our facts or circumstances the same or related` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(4) -- we may commence jointly` `are our facts or circumstances the same or related` IF `are our facts or circumstances the same or related`

-- s 44(3): "If ... the executive officer rejects an application or accepts an application on conditions -- (a) the
-- applicant may request the executive officer to refer to the Tribunal for a review"; (b) the officer "is to refer";
-- s 44(6): no fee.
DECLARE `What happened to my application` IS ONE OF
    `it was accepted without conditions`
    `it was accepted on conditions`
    `it was rejected`
    `it is not yet decided`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to my application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(3) -- I may have the rejection or conditions reviewed` `what happened` IF
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `it was accepted on conditions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it was rejected` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 45(1), (2): "When an application is accepted ... the applicant is to give a copy of the application to (a) each other
-- party; and (b) any other person entitled ...; and (c) any person to whom the applicant is directed"; (2) not required if
-- the executive officer gave or undertook to give a copy, the Tribunal dispensed with it, or the rules exempt it.
GIVEN `has my application been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the person a party, entitled to a copy, or one I was directed to give one to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has the executive officer given or undertaken to give a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has the Tribunal dispensed with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the rules exempt it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1), (2) -- I must give the person a copy` `has my application been accepted` `is the person a party, entitled to a copy, or one I was directed to give one to` `has the executive officer given or undertaken to give a copy` `has the Tribunal dispensed with it` `do the rules exempt it` MEANS
    IF NOT `has my application been accepted`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `is the person a party, entitled to a copy, or one I was directed to give one to`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent (an open list; s 45 says nothing of anyone else)
         ELSE IF `has the executive officer given or undertaken to give a copy` OR `has the Tribunal dispensed with it` OR `do the rules exempt it`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ss 48(2) and 53: what the Tribunal may do to a party who conducts the proceeding so as to disadvantage another party,
-- or who misses a properly convened compulsory conference.
DECLARE `What I did` IS ONE OF
    -- s 48(1): conduct the Tribunal believes unnecessarily disadvantages another party
    `conducted the proceeding to another party's disadvantage`
    -- s 53: did not attend a properly convened compulsory conference
    `missed a compulsory conference`

DECLARE `What the Tribunal may do` IS ONE OF
    -- s 48(2)(a)
    `dismiss or strike out the proceeding`
    -- s 48(2)(b)
    `decide the proceeding for the applicant, or strike me out`
    -- s 53(b)
    `decide the proceeding against me, or strike me out`
    -- s 53(a) alone
    `hold the conference without me`

GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did`
      `am I the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `did a presiding member and all parties present agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the Tribunal may do`
`ss 48, 53 -- what the Tribunal may do` `what I did` `am I the applicant` `did a presiding member and all parties present agree` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `conducted the proceeding to another party's disadvantage` THEN
        IF `am I the applicant`
        THEN `dismiss or strike out the proceeding`
        ELSE `decide the proceeding for the applicant, or strike me out`
    WHEN `missed a compulsory conference` THEN
        IF `did a presiding member and all parties present agree`
        THEN `decide the proceeding against me, or strike me out`
        ELSE `hold the conference without me`

-- s 49: after a dismissal or striking out under s 46, 47 or 48, "another proceeding of the same kind in relation to the
-- same matter cannot be commenced ... without the leave of a judicial member".
GIVEN `was it dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it the same kind about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a judicial member given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 -- I may commence again` `was it dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48` `is it the same kind about the same matter` `has a judicial member given leave` MEANS
    IF `was it dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48` AND `is it the same kind about the same matter`
    THEN JUST `has a judicial member given leave`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 49 bars only the same kind on the same matter after those sections)

-- s 55: evidence of anything said or done in a compulsory conference or mediation "is not admissible at any later stage
-- of the proceeding unless" (a) all parties agree, (b) it is evidence of directions or orders made there or their reasons,
-- or (c) it is relevant to a false-information offence, a s 100 contempt proceeding or a s 53(b)(i) order.
GIVEN `do all parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it evidence of directions or orders made there, or their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it relevant to a false-information offence, a contempt or a s 53(b)(i) order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55 -- it may be used later` `do all parties agree` `is it evidence of directions or orders made there, or their reasons` `is it relevant to a false-information offence, a contempt or a s 53(b)(i) order` IF
       `do all parties agree`
    OR `is it evidence of directions or orders made there, or their reasons`
    OR `is it relevant to a false-information offence, a contempt or a s 53(b)(i) order`

§§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- experts, witnesses, self-incrimination (ss 64, 66, 68)`

-- s 64(3): an order to pay the Tribunal's costs of an expert "does not apply in relation to a party unless, before
-- obtaining the assistance, the Tribunal advised the party of (a) its intention ...; (b) the likely costs ...; (c) the
-- likely amount of the party's payment or contribution, and gave the party an opportunity to be heard".
GIVEN `was I told of the intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I told the likely costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I told my likely share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64 -- I may be ordered to pay for the expert` `was I told of the intention` `was I told the likely costs` `was I told my likely share` `was I given an opportunity to be heard` IF
        `was I told of the intention`
    AND `was I told the likely costs`
    AND `was I told my likely share`
    AND `was I given an opportunity to be heard`

-- s 66(5): "A person who attends in answer to, or to comply with, a summons is entitled to be paid the fees and
-- allowances prescribed in the rules or, if none, ... determined by the Tribunal".
GIVEN `did I attend under a summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(5) -- I am entitled to witness fees` `did I attend under a summons` MEANS
    IF `did I attend under a summons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 66(5) speaks of summoned witnesses only)

-- s 68(2): an answer given, or the fact a document was produced, to comply with a requirement under the Act "is [not]
-- admissible in evidence in any criminal proceedings against the person other than proceedings for perjury or for an
-- offence against this Act arising out of the false or misleading nature of an answer". In those excepted proceedings
-- s 68 is silent (fork F7).
GIVEN `was it given to comply with a requirement under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it a perjury or false-answer prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) -- my answer may be used against me in criminal proceedings` `was it given to comply with a requirement under the Act` `is it a perjury or false-answer prosecution` MEANS
    IF NOT `was it given to comply with a requirement under the Act`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording
    ELSE IF `is it a perjury or false-answer prosecution`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: "(other than X)", s 68 leaves those proceedings to the general law
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Division 4 -- decisions and reasons (ss 74, 76, 78, 84-86)`

-- s 74: a decision "has to be given in writing ... if (a) [it] is a final decision; or (b) the Tribunal reserved the
-- decision; or (c) the rules state ...; or (d) a party requests".
GIVEN `is it a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was it reserved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the rules require writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a party requested writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 74 -- the decision must be in writing` `is it a final decision` `was it reserved` `do the rules require writing` `has a party requested writing` IF
       `is it a final decision`
    OR `was it reserved`
    OR `do the rules require writing`
    OR `has a party requested writing`

-- s 76: a reserved decision and its reasons "within the period of 90 days after the day on which it reserved its decision
-- or within an extension of that period given by the President". An extension is asked as the extended last day.
GIVEN `the day it was reserved` IS A DATE
      `has the President extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76 -- the last day for a reserved decision` `the day it was reserved` `has the President extended the period` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF `has the President extended the period`
    THEN `the extended last day`
    ELSE `the date` 90 `days after` `the day it was reserved`

-- s 78(1): if the Tribunal decides "without having reserved its decision and does not give its reasons ... in writing, a
-- party may, within the period of 28 days after the day on which the decision is given, request ... reasons in writing".
GIVEN `was it reserved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were written reasons given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 78(1) -- the time limit to request written reasons` `was it reserved` `were written reasons given` `the day the decision was given` MEANS
    IF `was it reserved` OR `were written reasons given`
    THEN `the step is not open to you`
    ELSE `the last day is` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day the decision was given`)

-- s 78(2): the Tribunal "is to give written reasons ... within the period of 90 days after the day on which it receives
-- the request or within an extension of that period given by the President".
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE
      `has the President extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78(2) -- the last day for written reasons` `the day the request was received` `has the President extended the period` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF `has the President extended the period`
    THEN `the extended last day`
    ELSE `the date` 90 `days after` `the day the request was received`

-- s 84(2), (3), (4): "A person in respect of whom the Tribunal makes a decision may apply ... for a review of the
-- decision if the person did not appear and was not represented at a relevant hearing" (not a compulsory conference or
-- mediation); the application "has to be made within the time limits specified by ... the rules" (not deposited: asked);
-- the rules may limit repeat applications without leave. s 93(5): after a no appeals election "any decision in the
-- proceeding is final and is not subject to appeal or review whether under Part 5 or otherwise", so no s 84 review
-- either (JUST FALSE: a flat negative).
GIVEN `was the decision made in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was a no appeals election made in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `did I appear or was I represented at the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `am I within the rules' time limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the rules bar a further application without leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(2)-(4) -- I may apply for review of a decision made in my absence` `was the decision made in respect of me` `was a no appeals election made in the proceeding` `did I appear or was I represented at the hearing` `am I within the rules' time limit` `do the rules bar a further application without leave` MEANS
    IF NOT `was the decision made in respect of me`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording
    ELSE IF `was a no appeals election made in the proceeding`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `did I appear or was I represented at the hearing`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF NOT `am I within the rules' time limit`
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `do the rules bar a further application without leave`
                        THEN JUST FALSE
                        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 84(5): "If on hearing the application the Tribunal is satisfied that the applicant had a reasonable excuse ..., the
-- Tribunal is to review the decision and may revoke or vary it".
GIVEN `may I apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the Tribunal satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 84(5) -- the Tribunal must review it` `may I apply` `is the Tribunal satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` IF
    `may I apply` AND `is the Tribunal satisfied I had a reasonable excuse`

DECLARE `How to enforce` IS ONE OF
    -- s 85: a certified copy and the person's affidavit of the amount unpaid, filed in a court of competent jurisdiction,
    -- free of charge; the order is then the court's order
    `file the certified order and my affidavit in a court of competent jurisdiction, free`
    -- s 86: a certified copy, an affidavit of non-compliance and a judicial member's certificate, filed in the Supreme
    -- Court, free of charge; the decision is then the Supreme Court's
    `file the certified decision, my affidavit and a judicial member's certificate in the Supreme Court, free`

GIVEN `is it a monetary order in my favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How to enforce`
`ss 85, 86 -- how to enforce` `is it a monetary order in my favour` MEANS
    IF `is it a monetary order in my favour`
    THEN `file the certified order and my affidavit in a court of competent jurisdiction, free`
    ELSE `file the certified decision, my affidavit and a judicial member's certificate in the Supreme Court, free`

§§ `Part 4 Division 5 -- costs (ss 87, 88)`

-- s 87(1): "Unless otherwise specified in this Act, the enabling Act, or an order of the Tribunal under this section,
-- parties bear their own costs". Where a costs order or the enabling Act says otherwise: NOTHING (fork F3; the order or
-- the enabling Act decides).
GIVEN `has the Tribunal made a costs order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1) -- I bear my own costs` `has the Tribunal made a costs order` `does the enabling Act provide otherwise` MEANS
    IF `has the Tribunal made a costs order` OR `does the enabling Act provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the order or the enabling Act)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 88(2), (3): the Tribunal may order a party to pay the costs of the proceeding; in the review jurisdiction it "cannot
-- ... unless (a) the party brought or conducted the proceeding frivolously or vexatiously; or (b) section 87(4) applies to
-- the party; or (c) circumstances have arisen in which the Tribunal could make an order under section 46, 47 or 48". (b)
-- is read as: the party did not genuinely attempt to assist the decision-maker (or, as decision-maker, to decide on the
-- merits) (fork F8).
GIVEN `is it in the review jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `did I bring or conduct it frivolously or vexatiously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `did I fail to genuinely attempt to help the decision-maker decide on the merits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `could the Tribunal act under s 46, 47 or 48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88 -- I may be ordered to pay the costs of the proceeding` `is it in the review jurisdiction` `did I bring or conduct it frivolously or vexatiously` `did I fail to genuinely attempt to help the decision-maker decide on the merits` `could the Tribunal act under s 46, 47 or 48` IF
       (NOT `is it in the review jurisdiction`)
    OR `did I bring or conduct it frivolously or vexatiously`
    OR `did I fail to genuinely attempt to help the decision-maker decide on the merits`
    OR `could the Tribunal act under s 46, 47 or 48`

§§ `Part 4 Division 6 -- more time, minor proceedings (ss 92, 93)`

-- s 92: the rules may let the Tribunal extend a time limit, even one in the enabling Act and even after it has passed;
-- (3) despite s 5 unless the enabling Act expressly excludes s 92; (4) the Tribunal "cannot extend ... if to do so would
-- cause any prejudice or detriment to a party ... that cannot be remedied by an appropriate order for costs or damages".
-- The rules are not deposited: whether they provide for it is asked.
GIVEN `do the rules provide for extending this time limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the enabling Act expressly exclude s 92` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would it cause prejudice costs or damages cannot remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92 -- the Tribunal may extend my time` `do the rules provide for extending this time limit` `does the enabling Act expressly exclude s 92` `would it cause prejudice costs or damages cannot remedy` MEANS
    IF `does the enabling Act expressly exclude s 92`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the enabling Act decides)
    ELSE IF `would it cause prejudice costs or damages cannot remedy`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `do the rules provide for extending this time limit`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the rules)

-- s 93(1) "specified amount means $7 500 and, on and after 1 January 2009, means $10 000" (as at the day the proceeding
-- commenced, fork F9).
`the 2009 change day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2009

GIVEN `the day the proceeding commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 93(1) -- the specified amount` `the day the proceeding commenced` MEANS
    IF `the day the proceeding commenced` `is before` `the 2009 change day`
    THEN 7500
    ELSE 10000

-- s 93(1) "minor proceeding means (a) a proceeding in which a monetary value can be ascribed to the matter in issue other
-- than (i) [where] that monetary value exceeds the specified amount; or (ii) a vocational regulatory body proceeding; or
-- (iii) a kind an enabling Act excludes; or (b) [a] kind that the regulations include ...; or (c) a kind that an enabling
-- Act includes".
GIVEN `can a money value be put on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money value` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the proceeding commenced` IS A DATE
      `is it a vocational regulatory proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does an enabling Act exclude this kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `do the regulations or an enabling Act include this kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(1) -- it is a minor proceeding` `can a money value be put on the matter` `the money value` `the day the proceeding commenced` `is it a vocational regulatory proceeding` `does an enabling Act exclude this kind` `do the regulations or an enabling Act include this kind` IF
       `do the regulations or an enabling Act include this kind`
    OR (    `can a money value be put on the matter`
        AND (`the money value` AT MOST (`s 93(1) -- the specified amount` `the day the proceeding commenced`))
        AND (NOT `is it a vocational regulatory proceeding`)
        AND (NOT `does an enabling Act exclude this kind`))

§§ `Part 4 Division 7 -- offences (ss 95-99, 103(3))`

-- s 95(1)-(4): failing to comply with a decision is an offence, but (2) not a monetary order; (3) "does not apply ...
-- unless (a) the Tribunal, in the decision, declares that subsection (1) applies; or (b) after a person fails to comply
-- ..., the Tribunal makes an order declaring that subsection (1) applies and the failure continues after notice of that
-- order is served"; (4) where the person had no opportunity to be heard, it "only applies to that person on the person
-- being given" a certified copy of the decision and a copy of s 95.
GIVEN `is it a monetary order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does the decision declare s 95(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was a declaring order made and served and the failure continued after it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I given a certified copy and a copy of s 95` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 95 -- failing to comply is an offence for me` `is it a monetary order` `does the decision declare s 95(1) applies` `was a declaring order made and served and the failure continued after it` `was I given an opportunity to be heard` `was I given a certified copy and a copy of s 95` IF
        (NOT `is it a monetary order`)
    AND (`does the decision declare s 95(1) applies` OR `was a declaring order made and served and the failure continued after it`)
    AND (`was I given an opportunity to be heard` OR `was I given a certified copy and a copy of s 95`)

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    -- s 95(1)
    `failing to comply with a decision`
    -- s 96
    `failing to comply with a summons`
    -- s 97
    `refusing an oath, affirmation, declaration or answer`
    -- s 98
    `giving false or misleading information`
    -- s 99
    `misbehaving, obstructing or interrupting`
    -- s 103(3)
    `breaching a condition of release after arrest`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 95-99, 103 -- the maximum fine` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a decision` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to comply with a summons` THEN 5000
    WHEN `refusing an oath, affirmation, declaration or answer` THEN 5000
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information` THEN 10000
    WHEN `misbehaving, obstructing or interrupting` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching a condition of release after arrest` THEN 5000

§§ `Part 5 -- appeals (ss 44(5), 93(5), 105, 106)`

DECLARE `Appeal` IS ONE OF
    -- ss 44(5), 93(5)
    `no appeal lies`
    -- s 105(11): a prescribed proceeding
    `no leave application unless you agree to indemnify the other parties' reasonable legal costs`
    -- s 105(1), (2)
    `with leave, on a question of law only`
    -- s 105(13)
    `with leave, on any ground of law, fact or both`

-- s 105(1), (2), (11), (13); ss 44(5), 93(5). NOTHING for a person who was not a party (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own
-- wording: "A party ... may appeal").
GIVEN `was I a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was it a decision on a s 44(3) or (4) referral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was a no appeals election made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it a proceeding prescribed for s 105(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `have I agreed to indemnify the other parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is it under a Schedule 1 or prescribed vocational Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does it deprive me of my capacity to pursue my vocation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Appeal`
`s 105 -- my appeal` `was I a party` `was it a decision on a s 44(3) or (4) referral` `was a no appeals election made` `is it a proceeding prescribed for s 105(11)` `have I agreed to indemnify the other parties` `is it under a Schedule 1 or prescribed vocational Act` `does it deprive me of my capacity to pursue my vocation` MEANS
    IF NOT `was I a party`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `was it a decision on a s 44(3) or (4) referral` OR `was a no appeals election made`
         THEN JUST `no appeal lies`
         ELSE IF `is it a proceeding prescribed for s 105(11)` AND (NOT `have I agreed to indemnify the other parties`)
              THEN JUST `no leave application unless you agree to indemnify the other parties' reasonable legal costs`
              ELSE IF `is it under a Schedule 1 or prescribed vocational Act` AND `does it deprive me of my capacity to pursue my vocation`
                   THEN JUST `with leave, on any ground of law, fact or both`
                   ELSE JUST `with leave, on a question of law only`

DECLARE `Appeal court` IS ONE OF
    `the Court of Appeal`
    `the Supreme Court in its other jurisdiction`

-- s 105(3): to the Court of Appeal if the decision was made by a judicial member or a Tribunal including one; otherwise
-- to the Supreme Court.
GIVEN `did a judicial member make or join in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appeal court`
`s 105(3) -- the court` `did a judicial member make or join in the decision` MEANS
    IF `did a judicial member make or join in the decision`
    THEN `the Court of Appeal`
    ELSE `the Supreme Court in its other jurisdiction`

-- s 105(5): leave "within the period of 28 days after (a) the day on which the Tribunal's decision is given; or (b) if the
-- Tribunal gives its decision without giving written reasons ... and the party then requests it to give written reasons
-- under section 78, the day on which the written reasons are given". Joined by "or", so either period is enough and the
-- later last day is taken, as for s 21(3) (fork F4); the period runs from the decision. Until the requested reasons are
-- given, (b)'s period has not begun, so an application can still be made. s 105(7): the court may extend, even after the
-- time has passed (asked as the extended last day).
GIVEN `the day the decision was given` IS A DATE
      `did I request written reasons under s 78` IS A BOOLEAN
      `have the written reasons been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written reasons were given` IS A DATE
      `has the court extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 105(5), (7) -- the time limit for leave` `the day the decision was given` `did I request written reasons under s 78` `have the written reasons been given` `the day the written reasons were given` `has the court extended the time` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF `has the court extended the time`
    THEN `the last day is` `the extended last day`
    ELSE IF `did I request written reasons under s 78`
         THEN IF `have the written reasons been given`
              THEN `the last day is` (`the later of` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day the decision was given`) `and` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day the written reasons were given`))
              ELSE `no time limit runs yet`
         ELSE `the last day is` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day the decision was given`)

-- s 105(6): "If leave is granted, the appeal has to be instituted ... within the period of 21 days after the day on which
-- leave is granted"; s 105(7) extension.
GIVEN `has leave been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day leave was granted` IS A DATE
      `has the court extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 105(6), (7) -- the time limit to institute the appeal` `has leave been granted` `the day leave was granted` `has the court extended the time` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF NOT `has leave been granted`
    THEN `the step is not open to you`
    ELSE IF `has the court extended the time`
         THEN `the last day is` `the extended last day`
         ELSE `the last day is` (`the date` 21 `days after` `the day leave was granted`)

-- s 106(2): "Subject to any order made by the Supreme Court, an appeal does not affect the operation of the decision".
-- TRUE means the decision is stayed.
GIVEN `has the Supreme Court stayed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106 -- the decision is stayed by the appeal` `has the Supreme Court stayed the decision` IF `has the Supreme Court stayed the decision`
